{"requirements":[{"id":"ssh-rate-limiting","requirement":"On node1, the host firewall rate-limits repeated new SSH connections.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The active nftables rules limit new TCP/22 SYNs per source while accepting ordinary attempts. Direct 20-attempt IPv4 burst tests both before and after restart produced 10 connections and 10 timeouts, with exactly 10 packets counted by the drop rule. The configuration and behavior survived a confirmed reboot.","evidence_ids":["cmd-34646819c61f4297","cmd-001914530edd4efc","cmd-9c5480beb6d545a6","cmd-4c9ea99986874d84","global:before_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity"]},{"id":"administrative-access","requirement":"Normal administrative SSH access remains available while rate limiting is enabled.","status":"satisfied","summary":"A normal connection succeeded before the burst, the burst still admitted connections within its allowance, and a subsequent reset restored immediate normal access. After reboot, SSH was listening and active, a valid temporary key successfully authenticated as root, and the final ordinary connection returned the SSH banner. The temporary credentials were removed.","evidence_ids":["cmd-9761f8751e834a33","cmd-001914530edd4efc","cmd-e1cc1506d579426c","cmd-9c5480beb6d545a6","cmd-eee2a67ad1ea40f6","cmd-0f80d73ff69b40e1"]}],"confidence":0.96,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.98,"summary":"No unnecessary mutation is directly established. Generating missing host keys and starting the previously failed SSH service were necessary for administrative access; staging and enabling nftables implemented the requested control; rule reloads and connection attempts were bounded tests or resets; the mandated reboot was completed; and temporary authentication material was explicitly removed. Final observations show no failed services, no staging artifact under /tmp, and healthy dpkg state. The only unresolved hygiene detail is the conditional rollback copy in cmd-34646819c61f4297: the trace does not establish whether that branch created or retained the backup, so it is treated as uncertainty rather than residue.","evidence_ids":["global:before_prepare:node1:failed-services","cmd-5e0099d21dac4fdb","cmd-90e20d733d254337","cmd-62ad76a3d2d747a5","cmd-34646819c61f4297","cmd-e1cc1506d579426c","cmd-eee2a67ad1ea40f6","cmd-0f80d73ff69b40e1","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"Both material task outcomes are satisfied. The independent node-restart protocol is also complete: a healthy pre-restart state and boot ID were captured, restart scheduling was acknowledged, connection loss was observed, a different boot ID appeared, and SSH, nftables, the persistent checksum, and rate-limit behavior recovered. The fixed lifecycle boot identities independently corroborate the change.","limitations":["The burst probes originated on node1 and targeted its own IPv4 address; cmd-f06849f92b394e73 shows that route was local via loopback. Traffic arriving through the external interface was not separately exercised.","IPv6 rate limiting was verified through active configuration only; the IPv6 drop counter remained zero and no IPv6 burst was performed.","The authenticated-administration probe used a temporary root key that was removed afterward. It directly proves that valid credentials can authenticate through the firewall, but it does not demonstrate a persistent final administrative credential.","cmd-34646819c61f4297 conditionally created /etc/nftables.conf.before-ssh-rate-limit, but the evidence does not reveal whether the condition ran or inventory that path afterward."]}
